  "closed_execution_category": "Unix ancillary owner lifetime, mixed-rights exclusion, reaping-triggered cohort join and separate accepted-message owner execution, including opaque io_uring lifetime dependency",
  "implementation": [
    "Full actual OpenHandles travel in mixed/opaque rights. Already-shared sets keep their compact Arc slice. Original Files capture/publication is synchronized; opaque metadata preparation and final callbacks/destruction are outside membership locks. Close/reuse cannot retarget accepted rights.",
    "Deleted OwnerLedger/OwnerView, rights IDs, Owner/OwnerGraph variants, reaping APIs, local_rights_need_owner cohort gate, retained_message_owner and separate progress_owned/start_owned_local_message/batch owner execution. Existing graph cycle rejection and iterative retirement remain; no new coordinator/resource thread/global lock/guest memory barrier.",
    "Accepted endpoint, rights, credentials, current batch item and resolved destination retain original resources across backpressure, STOP/CONT, close/reuse, faults and partial completion. Existing worker/solo prepared decoder and wait/subscription path are shared.",
    "Solo/cold progress borrows the current original VFS resolver during the invocation; it is never retained in PendingIo or sent between threads. Avoids repeated private PathQueries construction, including on ordinary byte consumers.",
    "io_uring opaque lifetime retains its original RetainedFd without owner tokens/collection. Does not broaden actual opaque control or SQE execution authority.",
    "Native-Linux-verified signal correction: Unix stream EPIPE raises SIGPIPE unless suppressed; datagram and seqpacket EPIPE do not. Scalar/vector/message/batch and solo use the accepted endpoint kind. Positive partial stream batch raises once after the peer closes between actual deliveries."
  ],
