  "initial_failures_and_corrections": [
    "Initial fixture/tests assumed Unix datagram EPIPE raises SIGPIPE, matching the prior implementation. Native Linux rejected that assumption. Corrected fixture + source scalar/vector/message/batch/solo semantics passed both native Linux and real backends. Initial wrong-oracle 48-case logs are historical only and excluded from acceptance.",
    "A draft opaque io_uring test attempted to retain epoll/ring as SQE files, which the existing API excludes. Kept the original exclusion; corrected lifetime test uses an opaque eventfd, while the opaque ring is still used to test actual SCM graph-cycle rejection.",
    "Compile/style errors in the broad removal were fixed before acceptance (removed APIs, iterator lifetime, redundant closure, unnecessary unwrap/mut, let-and-return and bool assertion).",
    "Initial Linux sync omitted newly modified network_batch.rs; regenerated source sync list and reran the affected process/runtime checks. Final source hash receipts include every changed Rust file.",
    "First shared solo implementation built a private PathQueries VFS on every call, causing a large single-core regression. Replaced it with borrowed original resolver and removed unused byte-I/O pathname projections. Final backend matrix, CI and paired long controls use the optimized implementation.",
    "Under parallel outer Linux tests, unchanged seccomp tests expecting completion within one shared-budget epoch failed intermittently (trap marker, strict-read metric, parent-death metadata). Isolated failing tests passed. Unchanged full process assertions pass with --test-threads=1; production scheduling and assertions were not modified. The parallel scheduling issue is not claimed fixed.",
    "Root pin audit initially rejected intentionally uncommitted runtime; rerun passed after committing the runtime and pairing pins. Documentation/pinning did not trigger unrelated CPU/network/graphics replays."
  ],
